cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CausalLoss-Fin, please cite it as below."
title: "CausalLoss-Fin: splitting financial agent loss between decisions and infrastructure faults"
abstract: "A causal layer over the FinalityBench benchmark that intervenes on both an agent's decisions and on individual infrastructure faults - dropped, delayed, duplicated and reordered messages - and splits a policy's monetary loss exactly three ways into infrastructure, policy and irreducible shares. Includes a decomposition of a realised fault schedule into individually repairable instances, Shapley allocation across messages, minimal sufficient causes, and a planted-ground-truth suite in four strata including the overdetermined case."
